# The Software Architecture Specification is governed by its byte digest (WAR SAS §101): an
# accepted revision records sha256 over these exact bytes, and `war check` reports
# `sas.digest-drift` if they move. A formatter that silently rewrites a digest-pinned normative
# document is the thing this system refuses everywhere else, so it does not run here.
docs/sas/

# Warrant atoms are digest-bound: the contract digest and the generated WAR.md/WAR.json are
# computed over these exact bytes, so a formatter that reflows one produces `generated-view-drift`
# and, after authorization, a contract that no longer matches what was authorized.
docs/warrants/

# Gate definitions are read by a deliberately restricted YAML reader (OW-ADR-0003): flow
# sequences only, no nesting. Prettier reflows a long flow sequence into a block sequence, which
# that reader cannot parse — the file would still look fine and stop loading.
docs/gates/

# Generated by OpenWarrant and carrying its own DO-NOT-EDIT banner; the same reasoning as
# docs/warrants/ above, applied where the generator writes outside it.
docs/decisions/generated/
